      "notes": [
        {
          "stage": "SILHOUETTE",
          "why": "layout GRID from the EDGE_TO_EDGE recipe rot6-light (HOLDS); primitive RECT from the PLATE member — a filled rectangular slab — the heaviest mark either runtime draws. LINE..CUBIC are always stroked whatever stroke says.",
          "composition": "rot6-light measured ink 0.6794 with the PLATE probe, estimated 0.6794 for a PLATE mark (x1.00), against a DENSE target of 0.55",
          "member": "the direction names no mark; defaulting to PLATE",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].layout",
            "fields[n].primitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": "FOCAL_HIERARCHY",
          "why": "4 registers and sizeMax 26, both from the measured recipe rather than from a density word. Registers 1..3 carry the composition and register 0 carries the market.",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].sizeMax",
            "fieldCount, and the site budget"
          ]
        },
        {
          "stage": "NEGATIVE_SPACE",
          "why": "spreadMax 128 from the recipe. Spread is a CEILING the seed draws beneath from a bytecode floor of 16, which is why the recipe pins it on the later registers: unpinned, one seed in twelve draws low and is a centred island in a collection that bleeds.",
          "consulted": "fields[n].spreadMax"
        },
        {
          "stage": "RHYTHM",
          "why": "symmetry ROT6 from the recipe — it is a project constant and carries no per-token variety, which is why the recipe rather than a seed decides it; count widened to 4..22 because COUNT is the drive and the range IS the response",
          "consulted": [
            "fields[n].symmetry",
            "fields[n].countMin / countMax"
          ]
        },
